  "headline_finding": "Core cost identity (D_trial(E) = m-1 group additions) confirmed cleanly by both independent reviewers via Stages 0-3. Two of the hypothesis's own falsification conditions triggered: Stage 5's partial-locus prediction (expensive) was falsified as literally specified (near-complete splitting measured), explained by a Semaev-polynomial symmetry argument the Executor supplied and both reviewers independently confirmed -- though the Red Team found a MORE complete governing law (residue-class parity) revealing an additional locus outside the theorem's scope that also splits completely. Stage 6's labelling prediction (every reachable cell is S-extension) was falsified by one genuine S-prime cell (GOAL-SIG-001's panel arm), confirmed independently by both reviewers -- exactly the 'reachable positive' the source proposal named as the single most valuable possible finding.",
